|~ `::trail`, the kind of the path a failure flew, and the laws declared
   under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [D337]. ~|

:trail
  |~~ A trail is the path a failure flew: a frame for each step that
      raised it or handed it on, from the step where it arose to the step
      where it is read. `[1 "x" 3] | map ~(mul 2) !| trail` answers the
      frame of `mul 2`, which broke on `"x"`, then the frame of `map`,
      whose code broke on the element at `/1`; a step the failure skips
      joins the steps of the last frame.

      An error holds it under `:trail`, written as the failure flies, and
      `trail` reads it from an error at rest; the words of vectors read
      it, `first` the frame where the failure arose and `last` the frame
      of the level that reads it. It prints a frame a line where it holds
      two or more, a frame standing on one line whatever its subject
      holds. An error at rest written with frames under `:trail`
      resumes that path when `raise` raises it, and an empty trail is no
      path, the raise starting one at its own step.
      ::snippet~([1 "x" 3] | map ~(mul 2) !| trail)
      ::link~(::frame | doc) ::link~(::error/trail | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/errors | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps |~~ The frames, from where the failure arose outward. ~~| [::frame]
    | proves :holdsAFrameForEachStep
        |~~ A failure inside the code of `map` holds the frame of the step
            that broke and the frame of `map`.
        ~~|
        ~([1 "x" 3] | map ~(mul 2) !| trail | count | eq 2)
    | proves :joinsTheStepsSkippedToTheLastFrame
        |~~ A step the failure skips joins the steps of the last frame. ~~|
        ~("x" | add 1 | mul 2 | count !| trail | last | skipped | eq ~(mul 2 | count))
    | proves :printsAFrameALine
        |~~ A trail of two frames prints a frame a line. ~~|
        ~([1 "x" 3] | map ~(mul 2) !| trail | print | lines | count | eq 4)
    | proves :resumesWhenRaised
        |~~ An error at rest written with frames resumes them when raised.
        ~~|
        ~(!{:a 1 :trail ::trail[::frame[1 ~(pre)]]} | raise | count !| trail | eq ::trail[::frame[1 ~(pre | count)]])
    | proves :ElementKindNotTakenError/refusesAMap
        |~~ An element that is no frame is refused at its index. ~~|
        ~(::trail[{:step ~(add 1)}] !| get [~(type) /index] | eq [::trail/ElementKindNotTakenError 0])
